<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15091" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕchidna</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχιδνα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an adder</i>, <i>viper.</i> The Furies were said to have them twined
			in their hair; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hence: stipite te Stygio tumidisque adflavit
					Echidnis E tribus una soror,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 313</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Nom. prop.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Lernaea, <i>the Lernaean hydra</i>, <i>killed by
			Hercules</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 9, 69</span></i>; <i><span class="en">158</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. F. 5,
				405</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A monster</i>, <i>half woman and half
				serpent</i>, <i>the mother of Cerberus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4,
				501</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Echidnēus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <i>of Echidna</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Cerberus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 408</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
